<title>FRANCE: Pinault stock rises amid rumours.</title>
<headline>Pinault stock rises amid rumours.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rumours about possible changes in the ownership structure of the holding company of retailer Pinault-Printemps-Redoute drove the shares higher on Monday.</p>
<p>Pinault-Printemps' stock, which has risen close to 10 percent since the start of the year, was up 1.71 percent at 2,380 francs at 1210 GMT.</p>
<p>The rumours, which have been circulating since last week, relate to a possible sale by CDR, the state agency grouping bank Credit Lyonnais assets slated for sale, of a 17 percent stake in Artemis, the holding company for Pinault-Printemps controlled by Francois Pinault.</p>
<p>CDR holds 25 percent of Artemis.</p>
<p>Both CDR and Artemis declined comment.</p>
<p>Other rumours hold that Pinault-Printemps would buy out the remainder of its Rexel or bid for Compagnie Bancaire's Cetelem unit.</p>
<p>&quot;There are several rumours that have been around several days but we are making no comment,&quot; an Artemis spokeswoman told Reuters.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
